"TreeAI" - Hackathon Edition
1. Product Overview

Product Name: TreeAI
Description: A Chrome extension that uses built-in AI to generate a dynamic, multi-level hierarchy outline from AI conversation histories (e.g., ChatGPT), with theme-based summaries and quick navigation via a side bar. It enhances long dialogues by providing structured overviews, fast jumping, and accessibility features for visually impaired users.
Version: MVP 1.0 (Hackathon Prototype)
Release Goal: Functional demo by hackathon end, including GitHub repo, video walkthrough, and live extension for judging.
Problem Solved: Long AI chats are disorganized and hard to navigate; existing tools offer flat lists without intelligent summarization or inclusive access.
Unique Value Proposition & Differentiation: Unlike basic navigators or TOC, this extension leverages Chrome's on-device AI for automated, summarized hierarchies—shortening long prompts/responses into key points. Key sell points:

AI-Powered Intelligence: Local summarization for theme-based outlines, not just indexing.
Privacy-First: All processing on-device, no data upload.
Inclusive Accessibility: Voice-activated navigation and TTS for visually impaired users, filling a market gap.
Hackathon Alignment: Demonstrates innovative use of Chrome AI APIs (e.g., Summarizer for outlines), emphasizing purpose (productivity + inclusion) and technical execution (local AI integration).



2. Target Users and Use Cases

Primary Users: AI enthusiasts and power users (e.g., researchers, developers) dealing with complex chats; visually impaired individuals seeking accessible AI tools.
Secondary Users: Hackathon judges and general ChatGPT users for productivity demos.
Key Use Cases (Hackathon Focus):

A developer reviews a multi-turn coding chat: Activates side bar, sees AI-summarized hierarchy (e.g., "1. Setup > Dependencies (summarized: Install numpy via pip)"), clicks to jump.
Visually impaired user: Voices "Jump to debugging section," hears summarized outline via TTS, and navigates seamlessly.
Demo Scenario: Load a sample long chat, generate outline in <10s, showcase privacy (no cloud) and inclusion.



3. Key Features and Requirements (Hackathon MVP Focus)
Prioritize core differentiators: AI summarization for hierarchies, quick navigation, and basic accessibility. Non-essentials (e.g., multi-platform) deferred to post-hackathon.

Core Features:

AI Hierarchy Generation: Extract chat text (prompts + responses), use Chrome Summarizer API to create multi-level outline (e.g., Level 1: Main themes; Level 2: Summarized sub-points, shortening long text).

Requirements: Local, on-device processing; configurable summary type ('key-points' for bullets); auto-refresh on new messages; handle up to 50-turn chats efficiently.
Sell Point: Differentiates from flat lists by intelligently condensing content (e.g., "Long prompt summarized to: Query on error handling").


Side Navigation Bar: Collapsible panel displaying tree-view hierarchy (expandable nodes with summaries); search/filter by keywords.

Requirements: Non-intrusive activation (button/shortcut); color-coded nodes (e.g., highlights key insights); click-to-jump using DOM scrolling.
Sell Point: Seamless UX for quick access, aligned with hackathon's User Experience criterion.


Quick Jumping: Link outline nodes back to original chat positions.

Requirements: Use scrollIntoView for smooth navigation; fallback for dynamic UI changes.
Sell Point: Maintains chronological integrity while enabling logical exploration.


Accessibility Integration: TTS for reading outlines; voice commands for selection/jumping (using Web Speech API).

Requirements: ARIA labels for screen reader compatibility; simple voice mode toggle; adjustable TTS speed.
Sell Point: Promotes social impact, unique in market—addresses visually impaired users' pain of long text listening.




Integration:

Platform: Primarily chat.openai.com (MVP focus); extensible via manifest matches.
APIs: Chrome Built-in AI (Summarizer for core outlines; Prompt as fallback for custom structuring); Web Speech for accessibility.
Storage: chrome.storage.local for persisting hierarchies per chat URL (reload on reopen).


User Flow (Simplified for MVP):

Install/load extension on ChatGPT page.
Click icon to activate side bar and trigger AI summarization (<10s).
Browse summarized hierarchy; click/voice to jump.
Demo privacy: No external calls shown in network tab.



4. Non-Functional Requirements (Hackathon Priorities)

Performance: Summarization <10s for typical chats; low resource use (leverage on-device AI efficiency).
Privacy & Security: 100% local processing; user consent pop-up for data extraction; comply with OpenAI terms via opt-in.
Compatibility: Chrome v138+; desktop focus.
UI/UX: Minimalist, intuitive tree UI; dark/light mode; responsive design. Emphasize hackathon UX: Clean demo video showing before/after navigation.
Error Handling: Fallback messages (e.g., "Chat too long—summarizing chunks"); logging for judges' review.

5. Technical Specifications

Architecture: Manifest V3; content script for DOM extraction/navigation; background script for AI calls/storage; side panel for UI.
Dependencies: Chrome AI APIs (origin trial token); no external libs for MVP (pure JS).
Risks & Mitigations: OpenAI UI changes—use flexible DOM selectors; token limits—batch processing; accessibility testing—simulate with Chrome TTS tools.
Hackathon Deliverables: GitHub repo with code; 2-min demo video (setup, generation, navigation, voice demo); live extension for judges.

6. Roadmap and Dependencies

Hackathon MVP: Core AI hierarchy + navigation + basic TTS (no advanced voice parsing if time-constrained).
Post-Hackathon: Multi-platform; export features; full speech recognition.
Dependencies: Chrome AI Early Preview access; Cursor AI for coding assistance; GitHub for submission.
Success Metrics: Hackathon judging alignment—high scores in Innovation (AI use), UX (intuitive nav), and Purpose (inclusion/privacy); user demo feedback >80% positive.

This PRD refines the product for hackathon success, spotlighting differentiators to stand out in judging and potential store listings.